# Copy this file to .env beside compose.yaml and fill it in.

# ── Web app ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The domain the web app is served at, without scheme or path. Your reverse proxy
# serves it over HTTPS: an instance accepts a web app only at an https address.
# Browsers keep each account's device, its keys and its message history, under
# the app's domain: on a new one, every browser starts as a new device.
DOMAIN=
# Where the app listens, in plain HTTP, for your reverse proxy: 127.0.0.1:8081
# when unset. For a proxy on another machine, set BIND_ADDRESS to an address of
# this server that only the proxy reaches: ports Docker publishes skip the host's
# firewall (ufw…), so 0.0.0.0 serves the app in plain HTTP to anyone.
# BIND_ADDRESS=
# PORT=

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Klipy API key, which enables the GIF picker (https://docs.klipy.com). Every
# browser that loads the app receives it: it is no secret.
KLIPY_API_KEY=
# The image version. Unset, compose.yaml runs the latest release of its minor
# version and `docker compose pull` gets its fixes. Set it to pin an exact
# release (X.Y.Z), or to `edge`, the main branch, for testing only.
# PINAI_WEB_VERSION=
